From 755e3f0dc2023ffb8adaa9adeeb298cd8500530c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:51:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] LogarithmicStrainHandler built from the Green-Lagrange strain

The new constructors take the deformation gradient and the
Green-Lagrange strain. The eigenvalues of C - I = 2 E are computed
from the strain, so the Hencky strain keeps the relative precision of
small strains in single precision.

In this mode, the divided differences of the logarithm, used by the
conversions of the stresses and of the tangent operators, are computed
with log1p from the eigenvalues of C - I. They have no cancellation,
even when two eigenvalues are equal: no special case is needed.

The test compares with the construction from the deformation gradient
in double, and checks the stresses and the tangent operators in single
precision against a long double reference, with equal principal
values.
